      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "# \ud83d\uddbc\ufe0f ZMongo Content Pack V3 \u2014 LoadImage \u2192 Saved Pack\n\nThis workflow demonstrates a content pack with exactly four typed values:\n\n| Icon | Field | Alias | Type | Source |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| \ud83d\udcdd | Message | `message` | `STRING` | JSON |\n| \ud83c\udfb2 | Seed | `seed` | `INT` | JSON |\n| \ud83c\udf9a\ufe0f | Guidance Scale | `guidance_scale` | `FLOAT` | JSON |\n| \ud83d\uddbc\ufe0f | Hero Image | `hero_image` | `IMAGE` | Comfy `LoadImage` node |\n\n## \u2705 What this proves\n\nThe image is loaded by ComfyUI's official `LoadImage` node, injected into the V3 content pack by `ZMongo Content Pack Add Image V3`, saved into the content pack as inline PNG base64, loaded back from Local File Store, and extracted again as a real Comfy `IMAGE` tensor.\n\n## \ud83e\udded Run steps\n\n1. Select an image in the **00 Load Image** node.\n2. Run the workflow.\n3. Confirm the manifest includes `hero_image` as `IMAGE`.\n4. Confirm the final `PreviewImage` displays the loaded image after save/load.\n"
      ],
      "title": "\ud83d\udcd8 README: Load Image Saved Inside Content Pack",
      "color": "#232",
      "bgcolor": "#353"
    },
